WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.687
One afternoon Anne happily walked home from school.

2
00:00:05.688 --> 00:00:09.611
"What a nice month November has been!" she said.

3
00:00:09.612 --> 00:00:14.379
Anne had never quite stopped her childhood habit of talking to herself.

4
00:00:14.380 --> 00:00:20.027
When she arrived at Green Gables, she found Marilla in the yard, looking very anxious.

5
00:00:20.028 --> 00:00:24.494
"Anne, Dora is lost!" cried Marilla.

6
00:00:24.495 --> 00:00:31.232
"Dora! Lost?" Anne looked at Davy, who was sitting on the yard gate, swinging his feet.

7
00:00:31.233 --> 00:00:34.645
"Davy, do you know where she is?"

8
00:00:34.646 --> 00:00:38.438
"No, I don't," replied Davy.

9
00:00:38.439 --> 00:00:47.928
"When I left at one o'clock," said Marilla, "Dora was playing with her doll in the kitchen, and Davy was making mud pies in the yard."

10
00:00:47.929 --> 00:00:56.899
"Dora must be somewhere," said Anne. "She would never wander far by herself. Perhaps she fell asleep inside."

11
00:00:56.900 --> 00:01:04.625
Marilla shook her head. "I've looked in every room. But she might be somewhere nearby."

12
00:01:04.626 --> 00:01:09.047
A thorough search of the yard, the barn, and the orchard followed.

13
00:01:09.048 --> 00:01:12.617
Finally Anne and Marilla met again in the front yard.

14
00:01:12.618 --> 00:01:16.314
"Where can she be?" said Anne, worried.

15
00:01:16.315 --> 00:01:21.189
"Maybe she tumbled into the well," suggested Davy cheerfully.

16
00:01:21.190 --> 00:01:28.961
Anne and Marilla looked fearfully into each other's eyes. "She . . . she might have," whispered Marilla.

17
00:01:28.962 --> 00:01:32.483
The Green Gables' well was the deepest in Avonlea.

18
00:01:32.484 --> 00:01:38.567
Feeling faint, Anne ran to the well and peered at the tiny glimmer of water far below.

19
00:01:38.568 --> 00:01:43.047
She lowered a lantern into the well, but she did not see Dora.

20
00:01:43.048 --> 00:01:52.023
Anne breathed a sigh of relief. "It's all right, Marilla," Anne called. "Dora didn't fall down the well!"

21
00:01:52.024 --> 00:01:56.850
"Do you think Dora went to Mr. Harrison's house?" Marilla asked.

22
00:01:56.851 --> 00:02:00.484
"He's on vacation now, and there's no one there.

23
00:02:00.485 --> 00:02:04.080
Dora is always talking about his parrot."

24
00:02:04.081 --> 00:02:07.334
"I'll go over and see," said Anne.

25
00:02:07.335 --> 00:02:16.052
Just then Davy's smile disappeared and he quietly ran to the barn. Neither Marilla nor Anne noticed.

26
00:02:16.053 --> 00:02:20.333
Mr. Harrison's house was locked, and the windows were all closed.

27
00:02:20.334 --> 00:02:23.840
Anne stood on the veranda and called Dora loudly.

28
00:02:23.841 --> 00:02:30.441
Ginger the parrot was in his cage in the kitchen. He shrieked and swore fiercely.

29
00:02:30.442 --> 00:02:36.488
Between the parrot's outbursts Anne heard a small cry from the little wooden shed in the yard.

30
00:02:36.489 --> 00:02:39.369
Anne ran to the shed door and opened it.

31
00:02:39.370 --> 00:02:44.914
She saw Dora, sitting on a wooden box, her face wet with tears.

32
00:02:44.915 --> 00:02:52.627
"Oh, Dora," said Anne. "We were so worried! What are you doing in here?"

33
00:02:52.628 --> 00:03:01.206
"Davy and I came over to see Ginger," sobbed Dora, "but we couldn't see Ginger through the window.

34
00:03:01.207 --> 00:03:10.601
"Then Davy brought me here," Dora continued, "and he ran out and shut the door, and I couldn't get out!

35
00:03:10.602 --> 00:03:18.361
Oh, I'm so hungry and cold, and I thought you'd never come, Anne."

36
00:03:18.362 --> 00:03:27.763
"Davy?" Anne said, shocked. She carried Dora home with a heavy heart. Davy had lied to her.

37
00:03:27.764 --> 00:03:33.939
Anne had grown to love Davy dearly, and it hurt her to discover that he had deliberately lied.

38
00:03:33.940 --> 00:03:38.768
Once they were home, Anne gave Dora some dinner and put her to bed.

39
00:03:38.769 --> 00:03:46.096
Marilla came grimly into the house with Davy, whom she had found hiding in the darkest corner of the barn.

40
00:03:46.097 --> 00:03:49.782
Davy looked up at Anne, hopeful that she might forgive him.

41
00:03:49.783 --> 00:03:53.548
But there was no trace of a smile in Anne's eyes.

42
00:03:53.549 --> 00:03:58.085
"How could you do this, Davy?" Anne asked sorrowfully.

43
00:03:58.086 --> 00:04:01.072
"I just did it for fun," said Davy.

44
00:04:01.073 --> 00:04:07.085
"Things have been so quiet around here, I thought it would be fun to give you and Marilla a big scare."

45
00:04:07.086 --> 00:04:12.332
"It wasn't fun, Davy," said Anne. "And you lied."

46
00:04:12.333 --> 00:04:21.043
"Of course I did!" said Davy. "If I hadn't lied, you wouldn't have been scared. I had to lie."

47
00:04:21.044 --> 00:04:27.448
"Oh, Davy, how could you?" Anne said. She had tears in her eyes.

48
00:04:27.449 --> 00:04:30.715
"Don't you know how wrong it was?"

49
00:04:30.716 --> 00:04:36.485
Davy was suddenly horrified. He had made Anne cry.

50
00:04:36.486 --> 00:04:42.234
Marilla left the room, and Davy rushed to Anne and flung his arms around her neck.

51
00:04:42.235 --> 00:04:46.662
"I didn't know it was wrong to tell lies," he sobbed.

52
00:04:46.663 --> 00:04:48.793
"How could I know it was wrong?

53
00:04:48.794 --> 00:04:55.461
Now you'll never love me . . . and I'm sure Paul Irving never tells lies.

54
00:04:55.462 --> 00:04:59.546
I'm trying to be as good as him."

55
00:04:59.547 --> 00:05:06.172
When Davy was convinced that Anne had finally forgiven him, he apologized to Marilla and went to bed.

56
00:05:06.173 --> 00:05:13.538
Later Marilla exclaimed to Anne, "What will we do with him? He's so naughty!"

57
00:05:13.539 --> 00:05:20.847
"Oh, don't say that, Marilla. Remember how bad I was when I first came here?" replied Anne.

58
00:05:20.848 --> 00:05:30.995
Marilla smiled. Anne, of course, did have a point.

